"""
The certificate tool of Wolly: keys, certificates from an ACME
server through http-01, and the question whether a certificate is due.

    acme newkey KEYFILE
    acme obtain DIRECTORY CAFILE ACCOUNTKEY DOMAINKEY WEBROOT NAMES OUT [private]
    acme due CERTFILE

newkey writes a new P-256 key, mode 0600, never over a file.  obtain asks
the server at the https URL DIRECTORY for a certificate for the DNS names
NAMES, separated by commas, and writes the chain to OUT (new, mode 0644);
the last word, private, allows a server on a private address and is for
tests.  due prints "due" when the certificate in CERTFILE should be renewed
(it ends within 30 days, or is no certificate) and "not due" when it
should not.  The tool prints one line, exits 0 on success and 1 on a
failure or wrong arguments.
"""
module Wolly.Example.Acme is
    """
    The command of the arguments.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
